<title>RUSSIA: SOCCER-RUSSIA BEAT LUXEMBOURG 3-0 IN WORLD CUP QUALIFIER.</title>
<headline>SOCCER-RUSSIA BEAT LUXEMBOURG 3-0 IN WORLD CUP QUALIFIER.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1997-04-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Russia beat Luxembourg 3-0 in</p>
<p>their World Cup soccer European group five qualifier on</p>
<p>Wednesday.</p>
<p>Scorers: Valery Kechinov 20, Sergei Grishin 58, Igor</p>
<p>Simutenkov 60</p>
<p>Sent off:</p>
<p>Luxembourg - Jeff Strasser 59</p>
<p>    Standings     P   W   D   L   F   A   Pts</p>
<p> 1. Israel	  6   4   1   1   9   4    13</p>
<p> 2. Russia	  5   3   2   0  13   2    11</p>
<p> 3. Bulgaria	4   3   0   1  10   5     9</p>
<p> 4. Cyprus	  6   1   1   4   5  14     4</p>
<p> 5. Luxembourg    5   0   0   5   1  13     0</p>
<p>Attendance: 10,000</p>
<p>Teams:</p>
<p>Russia - 1-Sergei Ovchinnikov; 2-Vladislav Radimov (16-Denis</p>
<p>Zubko, 65th minute), 3-Yuri Kovtun, 5-Omari Tetradze (14-Dmitry</p>
<p>Popov, 25), 4-Alexei Kosolapov, 6-Igor Chugaynov, 7-Viktor</p>
<p>Onopko, 10-Valery Kechinov, 8-Dmitry Alenichev, 11-Igor</p>
<p>Simutenkov, 9-Vladimir Beschastnykh</p>
<p>Luxembourg - 1-Paul Koch; 2-Jean Vanek, 3-Patrick Posing,</p>
<p>4-Marc Birsens, 8-Carlo Weis, 5-Jeff Strasser, 11-Frank Deville,</p>
<p>7-Guy Hellers, 10-Manual Cardoni (14-Marc Lamborelle, 70),</p>
<p>6-Jeff Saibene (16-Paolo Amodio, 87), 9-Roby Langers (17-Serge</p>
<p>Thill 65).</p>
